<title>POLAND: Celuloza up at PLN 21.5 on bourse debut.</title>
<headline>Celuloza up at PLN 21.5 on bourse debut.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's largest paper firm Celuloza Swiecie SA started trade on the Warsaw bourse at 21.5 zlotys, 4.9 percent above Tuesday's public offering strike price of 20.5 zlotys.  </p>
<p>The price was roughly in line with analysts expectations who saw the stock opening just above its issue price.</p>
<p>The state treasury sold 7.5 million shares or 15 percent of Celuloza at a special bourse session on Tuesday and the offering was oversubscribed. The average allotment rate was 34.64 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
